One of the most common DevOps interview questions:

“What is the difference between Blue-Green and Rolling Deployment?”

Most people explain definitions.

Strong engineers explain impact.

Blue-Green Deployment means you have two environments.

Blue is the current live version.
Green is the new version.

You deploy to Green, test it, and switch traffic when ready.

If something goes wrong, you switch back instantly.

Rolling Deployment means updating the application gradually.

Old instances are replaced step by step with new ones.

No downtime, but rollback takes time.

Simple way to remember:

Blue-Green → instant switch, easy rollback
Rolling → gradual update, slower rollback

When to use:

Blue-Green when zero downtime and quick rollback are critical
Rolling when resources are limited and gradual updates are acceptable
